<rml>
<head>
	<title>Confirmation</title>

	<!--
		A confirmation dialog: the one screen every game needs and nobody wants to write.

		Copy into your own UI/screens/ and edit. The parts worth keeping:
		  - the dialog is a child of .modal-scrim, which is what centres it. A scrim beside the dialog
		    dims the dialog too
		  - .is-inert on the content behind, which takes it out of navigation as well as out of the
		    mouse's reach. Without it the first direction press walks the buttons behind the dialog,
		    because a fresh document focuses nothing and its own nav finds the first tabbable element
		    in document order
		  - the *safe* action is autofocused, not the destructive one, so a player mashing confirm
		    cancels rather than deletes
		  - the destructive action is .btn-danger and says what it does, rather than "OK"
	-->
	<link type="text/template" href="/folio/lib/lib.rml"/>
</head>

<body class="screen s-pad-xl">
	<!-- Whatever the dialog is covering. Inert for as long as it is up; remove the class when it closes. -->
	<div class="is-inert x-fill">
		<div class="t-title c-text s-gap-m" data-loc="saves_title">Saves</div>
		<div class="btn-row">
			<button class="btn focusable" data-loc="saves_load">Load</button>
			<button class="btn focusable" data-loc="saves_delete">Delete</button>
		</div>
	</div>

	<div class="modal-scrim">
		<div class="modal modal-narrow">
			<div class="modal-title t-heading c-text" data-loc="confirm_title">Delete save?</div>

			<div class="modal-body t-body c-muted" data-loc="confirm_body">
				This cannot be undone.
			</div>

			<div class="modal-actions">
				<button class="btn focusable" id="cancel" autofocus data-loc="confirm_cancel">Keep</button>
				<button class="btn btn-danger focusable" id="confirm" data-loc="confirm_delete">Delete</button>
			</div>
		</div>
	</div>
</body>
</rml>
